    "description": "A multi-tenant SaaS exposes 120 REST endpoints over an Express/NestJS stack. Authorization today is hand-written inside each handler: some check a role claim, some check a tenant id, four forgot to check anything and were caught only by a pen test. The security team wants every request to pass the same mandatory checks (valid token, tenant binding, role or scope for the operation) before any handler logic runs, with one place that decides and a machine-readable reason in the logs for every denial. Handlers must not be able to skip the checks by accident, and adding a new endpoint must not require copying them. The decision to implement: how to enforce a uniform authorization decision on every incoming request before the request reaches business logic.",
    "decision_statement": "Enforce one mandatory authorization decision for every incoming request before handler logic executes.",
    "notes": "Intercepting-validator is the acceptable alternative when a reviewer prefers validation-flavoured naming."
